===BODY===
          <h2>A busy junction of motorways</h2>
          <p>Around Lille, the A1 from Paris, the A25 to Dunkirk, the A22 towards Belgium and the A27 towards Tournai all come together, and traffic is heavy at peak times. Many British drivers pass through on the way to or from Belgium, the Netherlands and Germany. A breakdown here is usually not far from home: it's only around an hour and a quarter to Calais.</p>

          <h2>Where we collect from</h2>
          <p>We collect from Lille and the whole metropolitan area (Roubaix, Tourcoing, Villeneuve-d&rsquo;Ascq), as well as Arras, Douai, Valenciennes, Béthune and the rest of the Nord and Pas-de-Calais. On the motorways, the official breakdown operator tows you off first. We then collect the car from their garage.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>We speak French:</strong> we can arrange collection directly with the garage or recovery company in Lille. Just send us their name and number.</p>
          </div>
===FAQ===
Q: How quickly can you bring my car back from Lille?
A: Lille is close to the Channel, so it's one of our quicker repatriations. We'll confirm the expected timing when we quote.
Q: My car was towed off the motorway near Lille. Can you collect it?
A: Yes. Send us the name and address of the garage it was taken to, settle any fees there, and we'll arrange the rest.
Q: Can you bring back a van?
A: Yes. We repatriate vans and light commercial vehicles too. Tell us the size and whether it's loaded.
